data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The user wants me to generate a title for a conversation. The user message is a directive about reading campaign context files and following input d002, then replying via cs-campaign-member.\n\nI need to:\n1. Use same language as user (English)\n2. Keep it brief, ≤50 characters\n3. No explanations\n4. Focus on main topic/question\n5. Remove articles like \"the\", \"this\", \"my\", \"a\", \"an\"\n6. Keep exact technical terms, numbers, filenames, HTTP codes\n7. Never use tools\n8. Single line\n\nThe key elements: campaign context, input d002, dispatch ID d002, cs-campaign-member reply.\n\nPossible titles:\n- \"Campaign d002 task execution\"\n- \"Following d002 campaign input\"\n- \"d002 campaign dispatch execution\"\n- \"Process d002 campaign input\"\n- \"Execute campaign input d002\"\n\nLet me check character counts:\n- \"Campaign d002 task execution\" = 26 chars\n- \"Following d002 campaign input\" = 27 chars\n- \"d002 campaign dispatch execution\" = 32 chars\n- \"Process d002 campaign input\" = 25 chars\n- \"Execute campaign input d002\" = 27 chars\n\nAll good. I think \"Execute campaign input d002\" captures the intent well - the user wants the assistant to read context and execute/follow input d002. But maybe \"Campaign d002 task execution\" is more natural.\n\nActually, looking at the examples, they tend to be noun phrases or gerund phrases. \"Execute campaign input d002\" is an imperative. Maybe \"Campaign d002 task execution\" reads better as a title.\n\nOr \"d002 campaign task execution\" - 24 chars.\n\nI'll go with \"Campaign d002 task execution\" as it's clear and natural."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789849365,"id":"chatcmpl-7f8d28a658464129a52013baee63c3c1","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

